<reference id="introduction" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Introduction</title>
   <shortdesc>The metR DOCX to DITA converter does not rely on visual formatting alone. It reads</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>DITA</keyword>
        <keyword>topic</keyword>
        <keyword>Maps</keyword>
        <keyword>constructs</keyword>
        <keyword>converter</keyword>
        <keyword>elements</keyword>
        <indexterm>DITA</indexterm>
        <indexterm>topic</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Maps</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>    <section>
      <p>The metR DOCX to DITA converter does not rely on visual formatting alone. It reads structural information from named Word styles and constructs. When those constructs are applied correctly, the converter and AI Agent can:</p>
      <ul id="ul_07233401">
         <li>Propose a DITA map hierarchy based on heading levels and topic relationships.</li>
         <li>Detect topic boundaries from heading patterns and semantic signals.</li>
         <li>Classify topic types: concept (descriptive), task (procedural), reference (tabular or lookup), or troubleshooting, and generic.</li>
         <li>Detect reuse candidates such as repeated phrases, shared definitions, and procedural steps.</li>
         <li>Infer metadata — shortdesc, product name, author, revision history, version — from field codes, document properties, and content context.</li>
         <li>Log and flag ambiguous or inconsistently styled structures for human review.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The converter reads the following Word constructs to accomplish this. Each is covered in a dedicated section of this guide:</p>
    </section>
      <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <title>Mandatory .docx constructs for conversion</title>
         <tgroup cols="3">
            <colspec colname="c1"/>
            <colspec colname="c2"/>
            <colspec colname="c3"/>
            <thead>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <b>#</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Mandatory .docx Construct</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Role in Conversion</b>
                  </entry>
               </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
               <row>
                  <entry>1</entry>
                  <entry>Title</entry>
                  <entry>Becomes the root DITA map <codeph>&lt;title&gt;</codeph> element.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>2</entry>
                  <entry>Heading 1 – Heading N</entry>
                  <entry>Drives the DITA map hierarchy and topic boundaries.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>3</entry>
                  <entry>Paragraphs (Normal / Body Text)</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> elements inside topic body elements.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>4</entry>
                  <entry>Tables</entry>
                  <entry>Converts to DITA <codeph>&lt;simpletable&gt;</codeph> or <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph>.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>5</entry>
                  <entry>Images / Graphics</entry>
                  <entry>Converts to DITA <codeph>&lt;image&gt;</codeph> elements with optional alt text.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>6</entry>
                  <entry>Ordered List (List Number)</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to DITA <codeph>&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;</codeph> or <codeph>&lt;steps&gt;&lt;step&gt;&lt;cmd&gt;</codeph> structures.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>7</entry>
                  <entry>Unordered List (List Bullet)</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to DITA <codeph>&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;</codeph> structures.</entry>
               </row>
            </tbody>
         </tgroup>
      </table>
      <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <title>Optional .docx constructs for conversion</title>
         <tgroup cols="3">
            <colspec colname="c1"/>
            <colspec colname="c2"/>
            <colspec colname="c3"/>
            <thead>
               <row>
                  <entry>
                     <b>#</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Optional .docx Construct</b>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                     <b>Role in Conversion</b>
                  </entry>
               </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
               <row>
                  <entry>8</entry>
                  <entry>Table of Contents (TOC)</entry>
                  <entry>Used as a structural cross-check for the bookmap hierarchy; not converted directly to a DITA topic.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>9</entry>
                  <entry>Preface / Notice / Copyright</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to bookmap <codeph>&lt;frontmatter&gt;</codeph> as a DITA topic.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>10</entry>
                  <entry>Document Properties / Field Codes</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to DITA map <codeph>&lt;metadata&gt;</codeph> and topic <codeph>&lt;prolog&gt;</codeph>.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>11</entry>
                  <entry>Character Styles (Bold, Italic, Monospace)</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to <codeph>&lt;b&gt;</codeph>, <codeph>&lt;i&gt;</codeph>, or <codeph>&lt;codeph&gt;</codeph> inline elements.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>12</entry>
                  <entry>Admonitions (Note, Warning, Tip, Important)</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to DITA <codeph>&lt;note&gt;</codeph> element with the appropriate type attribute.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>13</entry>
                  <entry>Cross-references and Hyperlinks</entry>
                  <entry>Maps to DITA <codeph>&lt;xref&gt;</codeph> element with appropriate <codeph>&lt;scope&gt;</codeph> and <codeph>&lt;format&gt;</codeph> attributes.</entry>
               </row>
               <row>
                  <entry>14</entry>
                  <entry>Math / Equations</entry>
                  <entry>Maps with <codeph>&lt;mathml&gt;</codeph> and or <codeph>&lt;equation&gt;</codeph>.</entry>
               </row>
            </tbody>
         </tgroup>
      </table>
    <section>
      <note type="warning"> If a mandatory construct is missing, mis-styled, or inconsistent, the
            converter either produces degraded DITA-XML or appends the content to the wrong topic.
            All content is always migrated; however, structural accuracy depends entirely on correct
            style application.</note>
    </section></refbody>
</reference>
